1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,578
From cocoon to cloth, in order.

2
00:00:02,578 --> 00:00:04,114
Harvest the cocoons.

3
00:00:04,114 --> 00:00:08,411
Stifle them, killing the pupa before the moth can break the thread.

4
00:00:08,411 --> 00:00:10,403
Strip off the loose floss.

5
00:00:10,403 --> 00:00:12,122
Cook them to soften the gum.

6
00:00:12,122 --> 00:00:14,960
Reel the filaments together in a filature.

7
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,500
Then degum, dye and weave.

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:22,864
Raw silk is mostly the protein fibroin, held together by the gum sericin.

